@*
    The empire's own settings, as distinct from its species'. A human empire is not called "Human",
    and the two are changed independently, so they sit in different places.

    Five things, each its own component: what the empire is called, what its ships are called, which
    scripted country flags it claims, whether it may turn up in somebody else's game, and whether it
    arrives already ancient. They are components because the lite card reaches for them one at a
    time — it names an empire by pressing its name, and edits the rest on the card itself — and one
    editor per thing is what keeps the two shells from disagreeing about any of them.
*@

<EmpireNaming />

<div class="sem-field">
    <label for="ship-prefix">@Session.Localizer.Label("SHIP_PREFIX", "Ship Prefix")</label>
    <ShipPrefixField Id="ship-prefix" />
</div>

<div class="sem-field">
    <label for="empire-flag-set">Special empire flags</label>
    <EmpireFlagSets Id="empire-flag-set" />
</div>

<SpawnToggle />

@*
    Whether it arrives already ancient. The designs file has carried spawn_as_fallen all along with
    nothing able to set it, so an empire written with it kept the setting and an empire made here
    could never have one.
*@
<div class="sem-field spaced">
    <label>Fallen empire</label>
    <FallenToggle />
</div>

@code {
    [CascadingParameter]
    public required DesignSession Session { get; set; }
}
